{"name": "write_file", "arguments": {"path": "parts/a2_06.js", "content": "{
emoji:'⏳',title:'The Time Capsule',start:'s1',
segs:{
 s1:{text:`It was a sunny Saturday. Four friends were playing in the old park near their school. Their names were Max, Lily, Ben, and Zoe. They were all ten years old. They loved to explore. "Let's look for treasure!" said Max. "Yes!" said the others. They looked under the bushes. They looked behind the trees. They looked in the old fountain. They found nothing. "Maybe there is no treasure," said Lily. "Wait," said Ben. "Look at this old oak tree. There is something in the ground near its roots." The children came closer. They saw a small metal box. It was half buried in the ground. It was old and rusty. "Wow!" said Zoe. "What is it?" "Let's dig it out!" said Max. The children dug carefully. The box was heavy. They pulled it out. It was a metal box with a lock. The lock was old. "How do we open it?" asked Lily. "Maybe the key is nearby," said Ben. They looked around. Max saw a small key under a rock. "Here!" he said. He picked it up. The key fit the lock. Max turned it. The lock opened. The children opened the box. Inside, there were old things. There was a letter. There was a small diary. There was a photograph. There was a coin. There was a ribbon. "This is a time capsule!" said Zoe. "People put things in it for the future." The children were excited. They wanted to see everything.`, choices:[{t:'Прочитать письмо',n:'s2'},{t:'Посмотреть на фотографию',n:'s3'}]},
 s2:{text:`Max opened the letter. It was old. The paper was yellow. The writing was beautiful. Max read it aloud. "Dear friend from the future," he read. "My name is Mary. I am ten years old. I live in this town. I am putting this time capsule under the old oak tree. I want you to know about my life. It is 1975. Life is different now. We do not have computers. We do not have mobile phones. We play outside. We read books. We listen to music on the radio. I love to ride my bicycle. I love to play with my friends. My favorite food is ice cream. My favorite color is blue. I hope you are happy in the future. I hope the world is a good place. Please write a letter back and put it in this box. Then bury it again. Someone in the future will find it. With love, Mary." The children were quiet. They thought about Mary's words. "1975," said Lily. "That was a long time ago." "Yes," said Ben. "Mary is old now. Maybe she is a grandmother." "But her letter is here," said Zoe. "It is like she is talking to us." The children felt a connection to Mary. They wanted to know more about her.`, choices:[{t:'Посмотреть на фотографию',n:'s3'},{t:'Прочитать дневник',n:'s4'}]},
 s3:{text:`Lily picked up the photograph. It was black and white. In the photo, there was a girl. She was about ten years old. She had long hair. She was smiling. She was wearing a dress. She was standing next to a bicycle. "This must be Mary," said Lily. "She looks happy." The children looked at the photo. "She is wearing a dress," said Zoe. "Girls wore dresses all the time in the past." "And look at her bicycle," said Max. "It is different from our bikes. It has a big front wheel." "Yes," said Ben. "Bicycles were different in 1975." The children looked at the photo for a long time. They tried to imagine Mary's life. "I wonder what she is doing now," said Lily. "Maybe she is a teacher," said Zoe. "Maybe she is a doctor," said Max. "Maybe she is a grandma," said Ben. The children laughed. They wanted to know more about Mary. They looked in the box again. There was a small diary.`, choices:[{t:'Прочитать дневник',n:'s4'},{t:'Посмотреть на другие вещи',n:'s5'}]},
"}}
</tool_call>

